-- title:
--   Level-one glued class of an inertial displacement is a node unit
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ in the non-units of $A$, so that the residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $q$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$ over $k$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those rational affine geometric places at which the value of the geometric $j$-generator lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,k$. Let `data` consist of a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair of $q$-expansions of $j$, satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (C X^{q} - X)(C X - X^{q}) \pmod q$; let $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ assert the integrality of the two degeneracy embeddings of level $1$ into level $1\cdot q$, and let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for $A$, $q$, level $1$, `data`, `hKr`, with target $k$ and reduction the residue map of $A$. Then for every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside the decomposition group, and every place $V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot q)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $V$ is neither strictly first nor strictly second for $P$ (the two conditions relating the geometric-level Frobenius to the reductions $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$, $P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,V$) and such that $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V \in W$, given a proof `hdeg` that the divisor $\sigma \cdot \delta_V - \delta_V$ (the action being through the arithmetic semilinear automorphism attached to $\sigma$) has degree zero, there exists a degree-zero divisor $D$ such that: every place in the support of $D$ is strictly first or strictly second for $P$; the glue datum $P.\mathrm{glueData}$ of $D$ at the node pairs obtained from $W$ by the arithmetic Frobenius $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,k\,1$ is admissible, i.e. its two divisor components have degree zero and vanish at the respective components of each node pair; $D$ and $\sigma \cdot \delta_V - \delta_V$ have the same class in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$; and there is a family $\chi$ of units, indexed by those node pairs and valued in $\mathrm{Additive}\,k^{\times}$, whose node-unit class $(0,0,\chi)$ equals the class of the glue datum of $D$ in $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0$.
--
--   This is the level-one case ($N = 1$, total level $1\cdot q$) of the toric statement that, at a supersingular (annulus) point, the inertial displacement $\sigma \cdot V - V$ on the $q$-level modular curve admits a representative whose specialisation to the glued model lies in the subgroup generated by the node units, the purely toric part of the degenerate Picard group. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_goodRep_toPic0Pair_eq_zero_smul_sub_self_levelOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_goodRep_toPic0Pair_eq_zero_smul_sub_self_levelOne), where the vanishing of the two component classes is read off from the node-unit description.
